1
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,568
What's your department?

2
00:00:19,568 --> 00:00:20,720
Com Arts.

3
00:00:20,721 --> 00:00:23,167
Com Arts? It's fun there.

4
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:25,318
Nero likes people from Com Arts.

5
00:00:25,318 --> 00:00:27,601
We're making things awkward for Florence.

6
00:00:27,601 --> 00:00:29,104
No, Owen, it's okay.

7
00:00:29,104 --> 00:00:31,833
Besides, I'm not fond of the Ferells,

8
00:00:31,834 --> 00:00:34,274
but Nero, you already have an advantage.

9
00:00:34,274 --> 00:00:36,076
Because if there's someone you like
from Com Arts Department,

10
00:00:36,076 --> 00:00:37,733
I can act as a bridge.

11
00:00:37,734 --> 00:00:40,166
There's someone I like.

12
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:42,703
What's the problem
with that Jennilyn Mercado,

13
00:00:42,703 --> 00:00:45,219
I mean, Jenny.

14
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:50,266
Well, it's because
someone is sending her secret messages.

15
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,296
What's the problem?

16
00:00:51,296 --> 00:00:54,595
Should she talk to the person
and ask why he's doing that?

17
00:00:54,595 --> 00:00:59,533
Why is he sending her messages
if he has a secret motive?

18
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:02,700
<i>And what I can advise you is,
don't confront him yet.</i>

19
00:01:02,701 --> 00:01:04,802
<i>Give him time</i>

20
00:01:04,802 --> 00:01:09,699
<i>and eventually,
he will have the courage to face you</i>

21
00:01:09,699 --> 00:01:12,693
<i>and tell you what he truly feels for you.</i>

22
00:01:12,693 --> 00:01:16,900
I want you to cook Chopsuey for me.

23
00:01:16,901 --> 00:01:18,879
Is that all? No problem.

24
00:01:18,879 --> 00:01:19,926
It's just a small thing.

25
00:01:19,926 --> 00:01:23,285
You will be needing
freshly picked vegetables,

26
00:01:23,285 --> 00:01:26,807
because that's how Dona Ferell used to do it.

27
00:01:26,807 --> 00:01:29,176
You can go to the farm
early morning, tomorrow.

28
00:01:29,176 --> 00:01:34,074
From what I heard,
our produce is ready for harvest.

29
00:01:34,074 --> 00:01:37,558
I'll ask Nero to drive you.

30
00:01:37,558 --> 00:01:38,552
What?

31
00:01:38,552 --> 00:01:41,027
You assume too much, Florence.

32
00:01:41,027 --> 00:01:42,923
Who do you think you are? Jennilyn Mercado?

33
00:01:42,923 --> 00:01:47,125
Are you that beautiful
for him to have secret feelings for you?

34
00:01:48,351 --> 00:01:50,030
What are you thinking, Florence?

35
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:51,698
You're not going on a date with Nero.

36
00:01:51,698 --> 00:01:53,367
You'll just go to the farm.

37
00:01:53,367 --> 00:01:55,484
Why are you so concerned about your outfit?

38
00:01:55,484 --> 00:01:58,476
What's happening to you, Florence?

39
00:03:25,692 --> 00:03:27,718
Let's play some music.

40
00:03:28,655 --> 00:03:30,957
Don't you want to sing?

41
00:03:32,165 --> 00:03:34,701
I'm out of tune.

42
00:03:35,769 --> 00:03:39,139
It's not important if you're in tune or not.

43
00:03:39,139 --> 00:03:41,140
What's important is...

44
00:03:42,178 --> 00:03:44,303
you're beautiful.

45
00:03:49,644 --> 00:03:51,312
Let's go.

46
00:04:43,290 --> 00:04:45,324
The doves.

47
00:04:47,353 --> 00:04:49,543
Hey, hey, get out!

48
00:04:49,543 --> 00:04:51,409
Get out of there!

49
00:04:51,409 --> 00:04:54,534
This way, hurry! Get out!

50
00:04:54,534 --> 00:04:56,892
They don't want to go out!

51
00:04:57,655 --> 00:04:58,915
Go!

52
00:05:00,608 --> 00:05:03,343
You two, get out! Let's go!

53
00:05:06,823 --> 00:05:08,358
Let's go!

54
00:05:10,526 --> 00:05:12,022
The picture.

55
00:05:39,076 --> 00:05:40,377
Hurry!

56
00:05:40,377 --> 00:05:41,879
Hurry, the fire is getting bigger!

57
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:44,047
Hurry!

58
00:05:46,256 --> 00:05:49,125
Move back, move back!

59
00:05:49,125 --> 00:05:51,488
- Watch out, watch out!
- Water!

60
00:05:51,488 --> 00:05:54,692
- Water!
- Did anyone bring a phone?

61
00:05:54,692 --> 00:05:55,893
- Call the fire department!
- Call the firemen!

62
00:05:55,893 --> 00:05:58,395
- Call the fire department!
- Water!

63
00:06:00,506 --> 00:06:02,433
- Did anyone bring a phone?
- The water is running out!

64
00:06:02,433 --> 00:06:04,839
- What happened to my cabin?
- Hey, Nero, Nero!

65
00:06:04,839 --> 00:06:07,406
- My things! Let me go!
- Nero!

66
00:06:07,406 --> 00:06:10,107
- We can't do anything!
- You don't understand!

67
00:06:10,107 --> 00:06:13,744
My things are important to me! My cabin!

68
00:06:13,744 --> 00:06:15,266
- Stay here!
- Let me go!

69
00:06:15,266 --> 00:06:16,453
- Nero!
- My things!

70
00:06:16,453 --> 00:06:19,550
- Stop it, Nero!
- You don't understand!

71
00:06:19,550 --> 00:06:23,487
- Let me go! My cabin!
- It's dangerous!

72
00:06:23,487 --> 00:06:25,891
- Nero!
- Stop it, Nero!

73
00:06:25,891 --> 00:06:27,325
Stop it!

74
00:06:37,901 --> 00:06:39,502
Stop it!

75
00:06:41,029 --> 00:06:43,107
Why do you have this?

76
00:06:43,107 --> 00:06:44,741
What are you doing here?

77
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:49,142
What are you doing here?

78
00:06:51,648 --> 00:06:52,868
I'm sorry.

79
00:06:52,868 --> 00:06:54,017
I didn't mean it.

80
00:06:54,017 --> 00:06:56,642
All of a sudden there was fire.

81
00:06:56,642 --> 00:06:59,328
Nero, just calm down.

82
00:06:59,328 --> 00:07:00,958
Let's find out first what happened.

83
00:07:00,958 --> 00:07:03,863
Maybe all of this is just an accident.

84
00:07:03,863 --> 00:07:07,564
This woman destroyed a place
that's very important to me.

85
00:07:07,564 --> 00:07:09,166
How can I calm down?

86
00:07:09,166 --> 00:07:11,635
Tell me how can I calm down?

87
00:07:11,635 --> 00:07:13,813
I'm sure Florence didn't mean to do this.

88
00:07:13,813 --> 00:07:15,466
Hey Owen, stop it first.

89
00:07:15,466 --> 00:07:16,540
It's not the time to take sides.

90
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:19,309
What Owen is saying
is don't jump to conclusions.

91
00:07:19,309 --> 00:07:21,812
Maybe Florence has an explanation for this.

92
00:07:21,812 --> 00:07:22,855
You too.

93
00:07:22,855 --> 00:07:28,685
Stop it! Everyone should stop
and please, everyone, go inside.

94
00:07:29,386 --> 00:07:32,146
We'll talk about this
when everyone has calmed down,

95
00:07:32,146 --> 00:07:35,726
so we'd know the root of this mess.

96
00:07:35,726 --> 00:07:40,164
Believe me, Grandpa,
even if I have calmed down,

97
00:07:40,164 --> 00:07:43,628
I don't want to see the face of this woman.

98
00:07:43,628 --> 00:07:47,523
So please, kick her out, Grandpa.

99
00:07:54,878 --> 00:07:56,962
You better rest, Florence.

100
00:07:56,962 --> 00:07:59,398
We'll talk about this tomorrow

101
00:07:59,398 --> 00:08:01,718
so we can think clearly about this.

102
00:08:21,023 --> 00:08:22,313
Ouch!

103
00:08:22,313 --> 00:08:24,408
Ouch!

104
00:08:24,408 --> 00:08:25,909
Why?

105
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:31,215
I have a bad feeling.

106
00:08:31,215 --> 00:08:34,266
Something wrong is happening.

107
00:08:34,266 --> 00:08:36,773
Go and call Florencia.

108
00:08:49,973 --> 00:08:52,199
Hello, my child.

109
00:08:52,199 --> 00:08:54,771
Why don't you have a camera?

110
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:02,205
I'm in the bathroom, Mother, Father,
making number 2.

111
00:09:07,117 --> 00:09:11,081
Florence, have you given the rambutan?

112
00:09:11,081 --> 00:09:14,618
<i>Did the kids like it?</i>

113
00:09:15,792 --> 00:09:17,160
Yes, Mother, Father.

114
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:20,938
He liked it very much
and consumed everything.

115
00:09:20,938 --> 00:09:23,329
He ate a lot.

116
00:09:24,590 --> 00:09:27,751
Florence, you're lying.

117
00:09:28,705 --> 00:09:30,667
Go and turn on the camera.

118
00:09:30,667 --> 00:09:32,109
What?

119
00:09:32,109 --> 00:09:35,945
Father, I'm telling the truth.

120
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:40,617
Florencia, show yourself.

121
00:09:40,617 --> 00:09:43,360
Mother, Father...

122
00:10:02,756 --> 00:10:05,542
Nero, so you're here.

123
00:10:05,542 --> 00:10:08,345
I asked Dencio to look for you,
but we can't find you.

124
00:10:08,345 --> 00:10:10,217
Where did you go?

125
00:10:11,748 --> 00:10:14,331
By the way,
Florence was saying something about the...

126
00:10:14,331 --> 00:10:17,565
Sorry to interrupt, Don Ferell,

127
00:10:17,565 --> 00:10:20,591
Florence said she turned on the lights.

128
00:10:20,591 --> 00:10:22,693
And something suddenly sparked.

129
00:10:22,693 --> 00:10:26,029
No one is maintaining the cabin.

130
00:10:26,029 --> 00:10:27,497
That's the thing.

131
00:10:27,497 --> 00:10:29,711
But what is she doing in my cabin?

132
00:10:29,711 --> 00:10:32,080
She has no right to go in there.

133
00:10:33,065 --> 00:10:34,772
I agree.

134
00:10:36,084 --> 00:10:37,828
That was Florence's fault.

135
00:10:37,828 --> 00:10:41,795
She did not respect your privacy.

136
00:10:51,088 --> 00:10:53,038
But grandson,

137
00:10:53,038 --> 00:10:58,537
the reason she did it
is because she wants to surprise you.

138
00:10:59,154 --> 00:11:02,007
When she found out that you like rambutan,

139
00:11:02,007 --> 00:11:06,577
she asked her parents
to look for rambutan for you.

140
00:11:09,542 --> 00:11:13,020
Why are you defending her, Grandpa?

141
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:15,714
The truth is...

142
00:11:15,714 --> 00:11:20,851
despite what happened, I admire her bravery.

143
00:11:20,851 --> 00:11:25,355
She had the guts to reach out to you
and be your friend,

144
00:11:25,355 --> 00:11:29,996
not like your Grandpa
who became a coward to approach you,

145
00:11:29,996 --> 00:11:32,565
and left you all alone.

146
00:11:38,049 --> 00:11:41,387
The fact that she discovered your secret camp

147
00:11:41,387 --> 00:11:43,522
is very impressive.

148
00:11:44,258 --> 00:11:48,547
It means, she's not only cooking for you,

149
00:11:48,547 --> 00:11:51,617
she's making an effort to get to know you.

150
00:11:51,617 --> 00:11:53,283
I'm sorry, grandson,

151
00:11:53,283 --> 00:11:56,845
I won't agree to kick Florence out.

152
00:11:56,845 --> 00:12:01,736
I think it's time we learn to forgive...

153
00:12:01,736 --> 00:12:04,720
because if we don't know how to forgive,

154
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:09,332
we will not have a heart
deserving of happiness

155
00:12:09,332 --> 00:12:11,757
and capable of love.

156
00:12:19,801 --> 00:12:22,318
Resign?

157
00:12:22,318 --> 00:12:23,752
Yes.

158
00:12:24,432 --> 00:12:30,371
That's what my parents and I
have agreed upon.

159
00:12:31,134 --> 00:12:37,150
I committed a huge sin against you.

160
00:12:38,929 --> 00:12:44,334
It would be a hassle on your part
if one of your grandsons is mad at me.

161
00:12:45,226 --> 00:12:49,976
He might lose his appetite
and refuse to eat if he sees me here.

162
00:12:51,258 --> 00:12:55,178
So you mean instead of
asking for forgiveness,

163
00:12:55,178 --> 00:12:57,980
you'll just run away from your mistake?

164
00:13:01,313 --> 00:13:05,617
In other words,
you are evading responsibility.

165
00:13:06,781 --> 00:13:09,704
Your mistake wasn't done intentionally.

166
00:13:09,704 --> 00:13:12,129
Everything was an accident.

167
00:13:12,129 --> 00:13:15,698
I think I made a mistake
with my impression of you, Florence.

168
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:22,828
No, I'm very responsible
when it comes to my actions,

169
00:13:22,828 --> 00:13:26,009
and this is what I think
is the responsible thing to do.

170
00:13:26,009 --> 00:13:30,290
To face the consequences of
the actions that I made.

171
00:13:33,173 --> 00:13:36,753
What do you think, Serafica?

172
00:13:36,753 --> 00:13:39,643
I'm so disappointed, Sir.

173
00:13:39,643 --> 00:13:41,867
But I agree with you, Don Ferell,

174
00:13:41,867 --> 00:13:50,167
resigning is just an excuse
to avoid responsibility for her mistakes.

175
00:13:50,167 --> 00:13:53,503
There are just two people
that I hate in this world.

176
00:13:53,503 --> 00:13:57,908
The people who don't know how to
cross the street in the pedestrian lane,

177
00:13:57,908 --> 00:14:00,302
and the people who don't know
how to apologize.

178
00:14:00,302 --> 00:14:01,591
As in...

179
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,136
I'm sorry.

180
00:14:08,941 --> 00:14:11,188
I'll make a deal with you.

181
00:14:11,188 --> 00:14:12,950
Apologize to Nero first.

182
00:14:12,950 --> 00:14:17,227
Now, if he can't forgive you, then resign.

183
00:14:17,227 --> 00:14:21,364
I will even give you
a generous separation pay.

184
00:14:22,032 --> 00:14:24,403
But don't give up easily.

185
00:14:24,403 --> 00:14:25,936
Try it first.

186
00:14:25,936 --> 00:14:29,639
Give the people a chance to forgive.

187
00:14:31,429 --> 00:14:35,423
Do not underestimate
our power of forgiveness.

188
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:42,524
As the saying goes,
we all deserve a second chance.

189
00:15:08,603 --> 00:15:10,947
<i>Apologize to Nero first.</i>

190
00:15:10,947 --> 00:15:14,751
<i>Do not underestimate
our power of forgiveness.</i>

191
00:15:14,751 --> 00:15:20,656
As the saying goes,
we all deserve a second chance.

192
00:15:25,228 --> 00:15:29,366
Not everyone deserves a second chance.

193
00:15:29,366 --> 00:15:34,203
Why, does Hitler deserves a second chance?

194
00:15:47,854 --> 00:15:52,002
Me, I deserve a second chance.

195
00:16:20,517 --> 00:16:22,280
What are you doing here?

196
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:24,655
Didn't I tell you
I don't want to see you anymore?

197
00:16:26,005 --> 00:16:28,507
Hey, wait.

198
00:16:29,608 --> 00:16:31,617
I'm sorry.

199
00:16:31,617 --> 00:16:35,932
One minute... that's all I ask from you.
Just one minute.

200
00:16:42,213 --> 00:16:43,540
You have every right to get mad at me.

201
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:45,208
I shouldn't have followed you that night.

202
00:16:45,208 --> 00:16:48,845
I shouldn't have watched you talk and dance
with your doves.

203
00:16:48,845 --> 00:16:52,301
But you made me curious,
you were off to the woods in the dark.

204
00:16:52,301 --> 00:16:53,678
What will you do there?

205
00:16:53,678 --> 00:16:55,235
Who knows if you're a vampire or worse,

206
00:16:55,235 --> 00:16:58,121
you'll hunt for a unicorn
and then you will drink their blood.

207
00:16:58,121 --> 00:17:00,757
That's because you're a bit weird.

208
00:17:00,757 --> 00:17:03,931
But what I did was wrong

209
00:17:03,931 --> 00:17:06,963
because my curiosity is not valid enough
to invade your privacy, right?

210
00:17:06,963 --> 00:17:09,611
And in our world,
no one is respecting our privacy.

211
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:12,638
So I know that your space is important
so you'll feel safe.

212
00:17:12,638 --> 00:17:16,130
That's where you feel safe,
and you can be who you want to be.

213
00:17:16,130 --> 00:17:17,831
Thirty seconds.

214
00:17:20,964 --> 00:17:23,480
But the truth is,

215
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:28,351
I just want to make up
for all the kindness you did for me.

216
00:17:31,292 --> 00:17:36,200
I know that sometimes... you defend me.

217
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:39,129
If you're enjoying yourself
at the expense of others,

218
00:17:39,129 --> 00:17:41,431
that's not called fun.

219
00:17:41,431 --> 00:17:44,778
You call that being disrespectful.

220
00:17:44,778 --> 00:17:46,755
Who are you? Are you her boyfriend?

221
00:17:46,755 --> 00:17:48,588
Hey!

222
00:17:48,588 --> 00:17:52,919
I also know your vote of confidence
in my cooking.

223
00:17:52,919 --> 00:17:56,663
What do you think of Florence's home cooking?

224
00:17:56,663 --> 00:17:58,364
I like her.

225
00:17:59,529 --> 00:18:03,019
I mean, I like her cooking.

226
00:18:03,019 --> 00:18:06,186
And I also know your effort to cheer me up

227
00:18:06,186 --> 00:18:09,125
so I'd feel good about myself.

228
00:18:09,125 --> 00:18:11,127
It's you again.

229
00:18:11,127 --> 00:18:13,362
You even woke me up.

230
00:18:19,135 --> 00:18:21,737
Don't get tired of dreaming.

231
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:24,774
I also know the saying,

232
00:18:24,774 --> 00:18:28,461
"the road to hell is paved
with good intentions",

233
00:18:28,461 --> 00:18:31,364
but that's what I only want.

234
00:18:31,364 --> 00:18:36,236
For me to be able to make it up
for all the kindness you did for me.

235
00:18:36,236 --> 00:18:39,596
I'm sorry that I burned your bat cave.

236
00:18:41,558 --> 00:18:45,028
I hope when our paths cross again,

237
00:18:45,028 --> 00:18:48,159
you will no longer be mad at me.

238
00:18:48,159 --> 00:18:50,471
And you can see me as the person

239
00:18:50,471 --> 00:18:54,574
who only wants to make it up
for all your kindness.

240
00:18:57,653 --> 00:19:00,032
Thanks for the one minute.

241
00:19:15,270 --> 00:19:16,826
You have every right to get mad at me.

242
00:19:16,826 --> 00:19:18,361
I shouldn't have followed you that night.

243
00:19:18,361 --> 00:19:21,911
I shouldn't have watched you
talk and dance with your doves.

244
00:19:21,911 --> 00:19:25,491
But you made me curious,
you were off to the forest in the dark.

245
00:19:25,491 --> 00:19:26,769
What will you do there?

246
00:19:26,769 --> 00:19:28,397
Who knows if you're a vampire or worse,

247
00:19:28,397 --> 00:19:31,787
you'll hunt for a unicorn
and then you will drink their blood.

248
00:19:31,787 --> 00:19:33,967
<i>That's because you're a bit weird.</i>

249
00:19:33,967 --> 00:19:37,030
<i>But what I did was wrong</i>

250
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:40,124
because my curiosity is not valid enough
to invade your privacy, right?

251
00:19:40,124 --> 00:19:42,702
And in our world,
no one is respecting our privacy.

252
00:19:42,702 --> 00:19:45,061
So I know that your space is important
so you'll feel safe.

253
00:19:45,061 --> 00:19:49,227
That's where you feel safe
and you can be who you want to be.

254
00:19:49,227 --> 00:19:50,862
Thirty seconds.

255
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:56,563
But the truth is...

256
00:19:56,563 --> 00:20:01,343
I just want to make up
for all the kindness you did for me.

257
00:20:04,356 --> 00:20:08,378
I know that sometimes... you defend me.

258
00:20:08,378 --> 00:20:10,685
Who are you? Are you her boyfriend?

259
00:20:10,685 --> 00:20:12,426
Hey!

260
00:20:12,426 --> 00:20:17,420
I also know your vote of confidence
in my cooking.

261
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:19,255
I like her.

262
00:20:20,301 --> 00:20:23,904
I mean, I like her cooking.

263
00:20:23,904 --> 00:20:26,959
And I also know your effort to cheer me up

264
00:20:26,959 --> 00:20:30,162
so I'd feel good about myself.

265
00:20:32,241 --> 00:20:35,548
<i>What is she saying,
that I'm making her feel good?</i>

266
00:20:38,274 --> 00:20:39,838
I also know the saying,

267
00:20:39,838 --> 00:20:43,596
"the road to hell is paved
with good intentions",

268
00:20:43,596 --> 00:20:46,438
but that's what I only want.

269
00:20:46,438 --> 00:20:50,786
For me to be able to make it up
for all the kindness you did for me.

270
00:20:51,421 --> 00:20:54,803
I'm sorry that I burned your bat cave.

271
00:20:56,702 --> 00:21:00,092
I hope when our paths cross again,

272
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:03,320
you will no longer be mad at me.

273
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:05,599
<i>And see me as the person</i>

274
00:21:05,599 --> 00:21:09,715
<i>who only wants to make it up
for all your kindness.</i>

275
00:21:14,177 --> 00:21:16,963
<i>My wish is,</i>

276
00:21:16,963 --> 00:21:19,730
I hope the time will come

277
00:21:19,730 --> 00:21:23,619
when you won't feel
something lacking in your life.

278
00:21:24,363 --> 00:21:27,640
But when that day comes,

279
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:32,980
I hope you'll meet someone
who will knock on your heart.

280
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:35,730
That's my prayer.

281
00:21:36,933 --> 00:21:40,136
Son, let her in.

282
00:21:40,136 --> 00:21:45,674
So she'd know who the real you is.

283
00:21:48,745 --> 00:21:51,714
What if he really refused to let you in?

284
00:21:52,841 --> 00:21:54,202
I will just keep on knocking...

285
00:21:54,202 --> 00:21:57,827
Knock, knock, knock, until he opens the door.

286
00:21:57,827 --> 00:22:00,749
If he doesn't want to open the door,
I'll destroy it!

287
00:22:00,749 --> 00:22:02,959
If I need to sneak into the sidelines

288
00:22:02,959 --> 00:22:06,996
or peep out the window
so he'd let me in, I'll do it.

289
00:22:06,996 --> 00:22:09,432
If I need to shout, I will shout.

290
00:22:09,432 --> 00:22:14,169
Hey, let me in your heart!

291
00:22:32,432 --> 00:22:37,293
<i>Is she the kind of person you were saying,
who will come into my life, Dad?</i>

292
00:23:36,223 --> 00:23:37,514
Troy.

293
00:23:37,514 --> 00:23:40,890
I heard Grandpa Garp is making
Florence apologize to Nero.

294
00:23:40,890 --> 00:23:43,225
You think Nero will forgive her?

295
00:23:48,047 --> 00:23:50,984
I don't think so, because knowing Nero,

296
00:23:50,984 --> 00:23:54,087
he's one of the toughest guys that I know.

297
00:23:54,087 --> 00:23:58,476
Well, knowing Florence,
she can be quite persuasive

298
00:23:58,476 --> 00:24:00,777
especially when she starts
talking from her heart.

299
00:24:00,777 --> 00:24:02,044
Let's make a bet.

300
00:24:02,044 --> 00:24:03,156
Okay.

301
00:24:03,156 --> 00:24:05,195
As for Owen and I, game.

302
00:24:05,195 --> 00:24:07,140
What are we betting on this with?

303
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:08,914
I'll bet my car.

304
00:24:08,914 --> 00:24:10,620
Well, you wanted to switch cars, anyways.

305
00:24:10,620 --> 00:24:12,538
Game.

306
00:24:12,538 --> 00:24:16,743
Me? I'll bet the Rolex
that Mom gave me as a gift.

307
00:24:16,743 --> 00:24:20,476
Okay, give me your Rolex and your car too,

308
00:24:20,476 --> 00:24:22,843
you won't win anyway.

309
00:24:22,843 --> 00:24:25,398
- Let's see about that.
- That's true!

310
00:24:25,398 --> 00:24:27,903
Let's see who will win.

311
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,748
Mr. Dove?

312
00:24:57,567 --> 00:25:00,245
Forgiveness is an expensive gift.

313
00:25:00,245 --> 00:25:03,571
Not everyone deserves it.

314
00:25:03,571 --> 00:25:07,109
Is he saying I don't deserve his forgiveness?

315
00:25:08,149 --> 00:25:11,013
Does it mean he is capable of forgiving

316
00:25:11,013 --> 00:25:13,882
but he refused to give that to me?

317
00:25:16,856 --> 00:25:19,705
Your boss is too harsh, Mr. Dove.

318
00:25:21,874 --> 00:25:23,709
Let me answer him.

319
00:26:24,334 --> 00:26:30,267
[Forgiveness is an expensive gift.
Not everyone deserves it.]

320
00:26:52,782 --> 00:26:59,188
I spoke to him earlier,
but it seems he's still mad at me.

321
00:26:59,956 --> 00:27:03,685
And based on the message he sent earlier,

322
00:27:03,685 --> 00:27:07,188
it looks like
that fool can no longer forgive me.

323
00:27:10,633 --> 00:27:14,684
And, Mother, that's the deal
I made with Grandpa Garp.

324
00:27:14,684 --> 00:27:19,841
If his grandson can't forgive me,
I will just go home.

325
00:27:24,013 --> 00:27:29,904
But Grandpa Garp said that
if I will really go home,

326
00:27:29,904 --> 00:27:34,106
he is still willing
to continue my scholarship.

327
00:27:37,493 --> 00:27:41,412
Mother, Father, I'll just call again later.

328
00:27:41,412 --> 00:27:43,633
It looks like Grandpa Garp is asking for me.

329
00:27:43,633 --> 00:27:44,867
Bye.

330
00:27:44,867 --> 00:27:46,590
Love you both.

331
00:28:02,656 --> 00:28:04,106
Nero?

332
00:28:07,154 --> 00:28:09,155
I accept your apology...

333
00:28:14,322 --> 00:28:16,190
But there's a condition.

334
00:28:18,534 --> 00:28:20,168
Condition?

335
00:28:21,537 --> 00:28:23,505
You owe me.

336
00:28:25,474 --> 00:28:27,043
How much?

337
00:28:27,043 --> 00:28:30,079
Do I need to pay for your cabin?

338
00:28:30,079 --> 00:28:33,049
I don't need your money.

339
00:28:33,049 --> 00:28:34,817
Huh?

340
00:28:34,817 --> 00:28:36,785
So what do I owe you?

341
00:28:37,714 --> 00:28:40,450
You owe me three P's.

342
00:28:41,399 --> 00:28:44,727
Three P's?

343
00:28:44,727 --> 00:28:47,532
Human Development Program of the government?

344
00:28:47,532 --> 00:28:52,226
Or Public-Private Partnership?

345
00:28:53,179 --> 00:28:54,837
No.

346
00:28:54,837 --> 00:28:59,275
What I mean is, you owe me three favors.

347
00:28:59,275 --> 00:29:01,043
Three favors?

348
00:29:01,043 --> 00:29:02,778
Yes.

349
00:29:02,778 --> 00:29:06,115
When the time comes
that I need a favor from you,

350
00:29:06,115 --> 00:29:08,084
you can't turn me down.

351
00:29:08,084 --> 00:29:09,853
No questions asked.

352
00:29:09,853 --> 00:29:12,722
You will help me with the favor
I'll be asking you.

353
00:29:12,722 --> 00:29:15,024
What kind of favor?

354
00:29:15,024 --> 00:29:17,192
Anything.

355
00:29:18,561 --> 00:29:20,210
As in anything?

356
00:29:20,210 --> 00:29:21,878
Yes...

357
00:29:24,168 --> 00:29:27,703
Anything and any time.

358
00:29:27,703 --> 00:29:29,851
That should be enough replacement

359
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:34,060
for what you've burned,
and all the sins you've committed.

360
00:29:34,910 --> 00:29:37,580
All the sins?

361
00:29:37,580 --> 00:29:41,617
It's as if I've done a lot of bad things
to you.

362
00:29:41,617 --> 00:29:43,318
You don't want?

363
00:29:44,536 --> 00:29:46,204
Deal.

364
00:29:57,941 --> 00:30:00,302
Yes, Nero?

365
00:30:00,302 --> 00:30:04,306
For the first favor, come with me.

366
00:30:06,041 --> 00:30:08,344
Where are we going?

367
00:30:08,344 --> 00:30:10,412
Have you forgotten?

368
00:30:10,412 --> 00:30:14,832
Because of what you did,
you owe me three favors.

369
00:30:14,832 --> 00:30:18,402
No questions, and you can't turn it down.

370
00:30:19,188 --> 00:30:25,831
So when I say come with me, you'll go.

371
00:30:32,192 --> 00:30:35,362
Where are we going?

372
00:30:36,906 --> 00:30:38,982
Well...

373
00:30:41,834 --> 00:30:43,468
Let's go.

374
00:30:51,854 --> 00:30:54,723
For the second favor you'll do for me,

375
00:30:55,825 --> 00:30:57,692
can you dance with me?

376
00:31:09,010 --> 00:31:10,486
Wow.

377
00:31:37,967 --> 00:31:40,735
And for the last favor, I'll ask from you...

378
00:31:46,976 --> 00:31:48,844
Kiss me.

379
00:31:49,511 --> 00:31:51,913
Kiss me with love.

380
00:31:52,523 --> 00:31:54,017
What?

381
00:32:04,029 --> 00:32:07,008
What did you get yourself into, Florence?

382
00:32:08,565 --> 00:32:13,269
Three favors and you agreed?

383
00:32:14,770 --> 00:32:17,205
What if he asks for...

384
00:32:23,445 --> 00:32:25,581
Erase, erase, erase...

385
00:32:25,581 --> 00:32:28,495
Don't think of bad things, Florence.

386
00:32:28,495 --> 00:32:33,855
Besides, you won't agree
to do rated SPG favors.

387
00:32:35,141 --> 00:32:39,428
Stop it, Florence,
just focus on your job today.

388
00:32:39,428 --> 00:32:41,429
Focus on your job.

389
00:33:22,297 --> 00:33:24,833
<i>Thanks for your forgiveness.</i>

390
00:33:26,608 --> 00:33:28,904
<i>Why is she saying thank you?</i>

391
00:33:33,337 --> 00:33:35,472
Am I disturbing you?

392
00:33:38,608 --> 00:33:41,444
You're playing with your bird again?

393
00:33:45,794 --> 00:33:48,364
I'm sorry, Bro, I just can't help it.

394
00:33:48,364 --> 00:33:49,965
It's like a fruit from a tree.

395
00:33:49,965 --> 00:33:53,602
It's like a low-hanging fruit
with you and your doves in your room.

396
00:33:53,602 --> 00:33:55,604
Do you need anything?

397
00:33:55,604 --> 00:33:57,042
Nothing much.

398
00:33:57,042 --> 00:33:59,862
I was just surprised by what I discovered.

399
00:33:59,862 --> 00:34:02,480
So this is what you do
whenever you go missing.

400
00:34:02,480 --> 00:34:04,355
You're taking care of birds?

401
00:34:04,355 --> 00:34:06,081
Exactly.

402
00:34:06,081 --> 00:34:09,042
I thought you were doing something
whenever you were alone.

403
00:34:09,042 --> 00:34:13,472
So you made the playroom made by Uncle Nilo
into your bat cave.

404
00:34:13,472 --> 00:34:15,495
Nice bat cave, Bro.

405
00:34:15,495 --> 00:34:17,714
It's actually very cool.

406
00:34:17,714 --> 00:34:20,216
Too bad, it got burned.

407
00:34:21,056 --> 00:34:23,954
And to think of it, whenever you go missing,

408
00:34:23,954 --> 00:34:28,362
Aldus and I made a theory
that you transformed into a werewolf

409
00:34:28,362 --> 00:34:30,439
and looked for a victim at night.

410
00:34:30,439 --> 00:34:32,050
- Right Aldus?
- Yeah.

411
00:34:32,050 --> 00:34:33,943
You can't blame us, Bro.

412
00:34:33,943 --> 00:34:37,146
If your cabin hadn't burned down,

413
00:34:37,146 --> 00:34:41,351
we wouldn't know
about this cool hobby of yours.

414
00:34:41,351 --> 00:34:42,669
How can you do this?

415
00:34:42,669 --> 00:34:45,903
Are you like Robert Downey Jr?

416
00:34:45,903 --> 00:34:50,627
Wait, does Ironman have pet doves?

417
00:34:50,627 --> 00:34:51,795
No, It's not Ironman.

418
00:34:51,795 --> 00:34:55,231
It's the movie where he knows
how to talk to animals.

419
00:34:55,231 --> 00:34:57,975
Ah, Stuart Little.

420
00:34:58,935 --> 00:35:03,506
That's not Stuart Little,
it's Doctor Dolittle.

421
00:35:03,506 --> 00:35:05,174
Doctor Dolittle.

422
00:35:05,174 --> 00:35:07,377
It's the one
where he knows how to talk to animals.

423
00:35:07,377 --> 00:35:09,746
I think that's the one.

424
00:35:09,746 --> 00:35:11,697
So you know how to talk to doves?

425
00:35:11,697 --> 00:35:13,436
Tweet, tweet.

426
00:35:13,436 --> 00:35:18,021
Not just doves,
but maybe with different kinds of animals too.

427
00:35:18,021 --> 00:35:19,422
What are you talking about?

428
00:35:19,422 --> 00:35:23,953
I can't talk to doves, and I'm not Ironman.

429
00:35:23,953 --> 00:35:26,362
Relax, Bro, no one is calling you Ironman.

430
00:35:26,362 --> 00:35:27,633
Ironman.

431
00:35:27,633 --> 00:35:30,967
But it's still pretty cool that
you're taking care of a lot of birds.

432
00:35:30,967 --> 00:35:32,985
Yes, is that a superpower?

433
00:35:32,985 --> 00:35:36,258
I think you're eligible
to apply as an Avenger.

434
00:35:36,258 --> 00:35:37,907
Birdman.

435
00:35:37,907 --> 00:35:41,511
You don't need superpowers
to take care of doves.

436
00:35:41,511 --> 00:35:44,647
They are very intelligent,
and it's easy to teach them.

437
00:35:44,647 --> 00:35:46,001
Really?

438
00:35:47,216 --> 00:35:48,918
What's that?

439
00:35:48,918 --> 00:35:50,920
I use them to send messages.

440
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:52,322
Really?

441
00:35:52,322 --> 00:35:55,204
- Yes.
- So they can do that?

442
00:35:56,092 --> 00:35:57,727
But the important question is,

443
00:35:57,727 --> 00:36:00,863
to whom do you send messages using your pet?

444
00:36:00,863 --> 00:36:01,898
Yes.

445
00:36:01,898 --> 00:36:06,302
From what it looks like,
it's someone special.

446
00:36:06,302 --> 00:36:07,704
What are you talking about?

447
00:36:07,704 --> 00:36:10,105
If you don't need anything, you can go.

448
00:36:11,474 --> 00:36:13,876
Hey, where are you going?

449
00:36:13,876 --> 00:36:15,345
- Stop touching your birdie.
- Come here, Birdman.

450
00:36:15,345 --> 00:36:17,213
Hey.

451
00:36:17,213 --> 00:36:20,383
Is there anything else you want us to do,
Don Ferell?

452
00:36:20,383 --> 00:36:21,617
No more. We're fine.

453
00:36:21,617 --> 00:36:25,588
By the way, you and your staff can eat.

454
00:36:25,588 --> 00:36:27,389
Thank you, Sir.

455
00:36:29,625 --> 00:36:31,594
- Serafica?
- Yes, Sir?

456
00:36:31,594 --> 00:36:35,764
Can Florence join us for dinner?

457
00:36:45,430 --> 00:36:46,721
No thank you, Grandpa Garp.

458
00:36:46,721 --> 00:36:50,779
You might discover that I eat a lot of rice.

459
00:36:53,398 --> 00:36:55,200
Don't be ridiculous, Florence.

460
00:36:55,200 --> 00:36:59,671
Of course,
she'll be honored to join you, Sir.

461
00:36:59,671 --> 00:37:00,851
Very good.

462
00:37:00,851 --> 00:37:04,393
- Join us.
- Yes, I'll be honored to join you.

463
00:37:05,514 --> 00:37:07,597
Come on.

464
00:37:07,597 --> 00:37:11,333
Florence, why don't you join us?

465
00:37:12,424 --> 00:37:13,694
Okay.

466
00:37:21,306 --> 00:37:22,970
Excuse me, Sir.

467
00:37:22,970 --> 00:37:24,580
Okay.

468
00:37:28,259 --> 00:37:30,217
You don't have a knife.

469
00:37:31,687 --> 00:37:33,389
And you don't have drinks.

470
00:37:39,449 --> 00:37:43,066
Okay, eating time.

471
00:37:43,066 --> 00:37:44,667
Wait.

472
00:37:46,721 --> 00:37:48,890
Won't we pray first?

473
00:37:51,841 --> 00:37:53,926
Sorry, I'm just used to doing that at home,

474
00:37:53,926 --> 00:37:56,614
but if you don't practice that here,
that's okay.

475
00:37:56,614 --> 00:37:58,833
You might be from a non-sectarian family.

476
00:37:58,834 --> 00:38:01,168
No, no, no. We're not non-sectarian.

477
00:38:01,168 --> 00:38:04,572
Go ahead, it's a good idea actually
if we pray now.

478
00:38:04,572 --> 00:38:08,525
Will you do the honors to lead the prayer?

479
00:38:08,525 --> 00:38:10,176
Sure, no problem.

480
00:38:10,176 --> 00:38:11,660
Good.

481
00:38:13,887 --> 00:38:17,943
In the name of the Father,
the Son, and the Holy Spirit,

482
00:38:17,943 --> 00:38:19,114
Amen.

483
00:38:20,231 --> 00:38:22,001
Thank you, Lord, for the food

484
00:38:22,001 --> 00:38:27,266
and the chance for us to eat together now.

485
00:38:27,267 --> 00:38:32,869
But there are a lot of things
I am thankful for, not only for the food.

486
00:38:32,869 --> 00:38:38,066
Thank you that everybody who is eating here
is safe and healthy.

487
00:38:38,067 --> 00:38:41,190
Thank you
that we're not infected with the virus

488
00:38:41,190 --> 00:38:43,366
that can affect our sense of taste.

489
00:38:43,367 --> 00:38:45,810
But most importantly,

490
00:38:45,810 --> 00:38:49,583
thank you to the Ferell Family
who accepted me.

491
00:38:49,583 --> 00:38:57,607
That even if sometimes I failed,
they were able to forgive me.

492
00:38:57,607 --> 00:39:00,943
And now, I was invited to eat with them.

493
00:39:00,943 --> 00:39:04,814
You're really great, Lord,
so thank you so much.

494
00:39:04,814 --> 00:39:07,617
And if saying thank you is kage bunshin...

495
00:39:07,617 --> 00:39:11,521
Thank you times two, times two,
times two, times two.

496
00:39:11,521 --> 00:39:15,858
Never-ending thank you to you, Amen.

497
00:39:15,858 --> 00:39:17,593
There.

498
00:39:19,929 --> 00:39:21,697
So, can we eat?

499
00:39:21,697 --> 00:39:23,665
- Game.
- Okay.

500
00:39:33,127 --> 00:39:35,035
You won't eat rice?

501
00:39:36,279 --> 00:39:37,777
Grandpa.

502
00:39:38,625 --> 00:39:42,652
In two seconds, can you give ten fruits
that start with the letter F?

503
00:39:42,652 --> 00:39:43,986
F?

504
00:39:43,986 --> 00:39:46,028
One, two... Time is up.

505
00:39:46,028 --> 00:39:48,457
There's no fruit
that starts with the letter F.

506
00:39:48,457 --> 00:39:50,363
Fruit salad.

507
00:39:50,363 --> 00:39:51,824
Boom.

508
00:39:53,196 --> 00:39:56,339
- Cheating.
- Boom.

509
00:39:56,339 --> 00:39:58,433
Work smarter, not harder.

510
00:40:00,002 --> 00:40:02,738
You're so funny.
You inherited that from your father.

511
00:40:02,738 --> 00:40:04,073
I'll take that as a compliment, Grandpa.

512
00:40:04,073 --> 00:40:07,309
You should.
You shouldn't be ashamed of your father.

513
00:40:08,377 --> 00:40:09,679
How about you, Florence?

514
00:40:09,679 --> 00:40:11,663
How are you? Are you ready for school?

515
00:40:11,663 --> 00:40:16,915
Yes. Tomorrow is my day off,
and I'll be meeting my mother and father.

516
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:18,074
For what?

517
00:40:18,074 --> 00:40:20,339
We'll buy things for school,

518
00:40:20,339 --> 00:40:24,176
and I can also give my first salary to them
for father's medications.

519
00:40:24,176 --> 00:40:25,956
Good girl.

520
00:40:25,956 --> 00:40:28,764
By the way, send my regards to your parents.

521
00:40:28,764 --> 00:40:30,653
You know, they're very lucky to have you,

522
00:40:30,653 --> 00:40:33,672
and tell them that the family is very happy

523
00:40:33,672 --> 00:40:37,566
because you made us happy with
the nice food that you're preparing for us.

524
00:40:37,567 --> 00:40:38,724
My regards.

525
00:40:38,724 --> 00:40:42,875
Yes. Do you know that
I always talk about you?

526
00:40:42,875 --> 00:40:45,102
I hope everyone likes to tell a story.

527
00:40:45,102 --> 00:40:47,000
Not like our brother over there.

528
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:49,273
He has so many secrets.

529
00:40:49,273 --> 00:40:52,313
Grandpa, do you know about his birds?

530
00:40:52,313 --> 00:40:55,825
Yes, the doves...

531
00:40:55,825 --> 00:40:59,962
His father taught him how to teach the birds.

532
00:40:59,962 --> 00:41:03,930
Now, did you know that
it was me who taught his father?

533
00:41:05,359 --> 00:41:06,883
But not only that, Grandpa.

534
00:41:06,883 --> 00:41:10,227
- Huh?
- Nero's the romantic type.

535
00:41:10,227 --> 00:41:13,063
He's using the birds to send secret messages.

536
00:41:22,885 --> 00:41:24,784
Secret messages?

537
00:41:24,784 --> 00:41:26,221
Busted.

538
00:41:27,272 --> 00:41:31,393
So, Nero, who is this
special someone of yours?

539
00:41:31,393 --> 00:41:32,784
That's none of your business.

540
00:41:32,784 --> 00:41:35,113
Stop bugging Nero.

541
00:41:35,113 --> 00:41:36,549
Anyway, let's just wait.

542
00:41:36,549 --> 00:41:38,617
Give him time and space,

543
00:41:38,617 --> 00:41:43,015
I'm sure one of these days,
we'll find out who is that secret girl

544
00:41:43,015 --> 00:41:45,156
and what are the messages.

545
00:41:45,156 --> 00:41:46,808
Right, Nero?

546
00:41:50,012 --> 00:41:52,055
Maybe longer.

547
00:41:52,055 --> 00:41:53,548
Birdman.

548
00:41:55,512 --> 00:41:57,413
Longer time.

549
00:42:02,231 --> 00:42:06,360
Guys, have you noticed Owen?

550
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:07,540
Why?

551
00:42:07,540 --> 00:42:11,009
He's becoming close to Florence.

552
00:42:11,821 --> 00:42:14,086
I can see that as well.

553
00:42:14,086 --> 00:42:16,548
Do you think something is going on with them?

554
00:42:16,548 --> 00:42:18,118
Huh, that's weird.

555
00:42:18,118 --> 00:42:21,477
Remember, it was he who said
it's totally unacceptable

556
00:42:21,477 --> 00:42:23,412
if we fall for the cook.

557
00:42:25,165 --> 00:42:27,833
Guys, here we go again.

558
00:42:27,833 --> 00:42:32,243
After we bully Florence,
now we're thinking badly of her?

559
00:42:32,243 --> 00:42:34,298
She deserves some credit.

560
00:42:34,298 --> 00:42:37,829
Ever since she became our cook,
Grandpa Garp seems happy,

561
00:42:37,829 --> 00:42:40,969
and we look like a family that eats together.

562
00:42:42,147 --> 00:42:46,477
What I can only say, Bro,
you got to give her a chance.

563
00:42:46,477 --> 00:42:48,548
And once you get to know her,

564
00:42:48,548 --> 00:42:51,071
you'll see how fun she is to be with.

565
00:42:52,180 --> 00:42:55,563
Honestly, I'm okay with her.

566
00:42:55,563 --> 00:42:57,290
I'm starting to like her.

567
00:42:57,290 --> 00:42:58,547
Like her?

568
00:42:58,547 --> 00:43:00,448
As in, like her?

569
00:43:00,448 --> 00:43:02,350
Of course not.

570
00:43:02,350 --> 00:43:04,169
What I mean is,

571
00:43:04,169 --> 00:43:08,290
I'm starting to appreciate the good things
she's doing here at home.

572
00:43:08,290 --> 00:43:11,893
Not to mention that she does cook well.

573
00:43:12,827 --> 00:43:14,629
How about you, Aldus?

574
00:43:42,393 --> 00:43:45,695
<i>So, Nero,
who is this special someone of yours?</i>

575
00:44:03,156 --> 00:44:06,907
Of course, he won't admit
who his special someone is.

576
00:44:06,907 --> 00:44:09,234
It's just me.

577
00:44:09,234 --> 00:44:14,055
What will they think if they found out
that he has fallen for a cook?

578
00:44:14,055 --> 00:44:19,828
Wait, just because I'm a cook,
a Ferell is not allowed to like me?

579
00:44:19,828 --> 00:44:22,964
Because we're worlds apart?

580
00:44:22,964 --> 00:44:23,965
In the drama series,

581
00:44:23,965 --> 00:44:27,335
the lead characters from different worlds
always fall for each other.

582
00:44:29,804 --> 00:44:33,174
But it's a drama series
because it's not for real.

583
00:44:34,437 --> 00:44:36,778
Is it my fault that I'm not rich?

584
00:44:36,778 --> 00:44:38,613
Did I like that?

585
00:44:39,381 --> 00:44:41,516
And I don't want to be rich.

586
00:44:41,516 --> 00:44:43,952
The richer you are,
the more problems you have.

587
00:44:43,952 --> 00:44:46,388
And I'm happy with the kind of life I have.

588
00:44:46,388 --> 00:44:51,270
I will never replace Mother and Father
for a luxurious life.

589
00:45:04,739 --> 00:45:06,374
Hello?

590
00:45:06,374 --> 00:45:08,009
<i>Hello, Don Rogelio, Sir.</i>

591
00:45:08,009 --> 00:45:09,399
<i>This is Mark.</i>

592
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:12,981
<i>I've already run the aging program
that I told you about,</i>

593
00:45:12,981 --> 00:45:14,783
<i>the picture of Baby Celestina.</i>

594
00:45:14,783 --> 00:45:20,889
<i>I emailed you a picture
of how she will possibly look in 17 years.</i>

595
00:45:20,889 --> 00:45:22,657
All right.

596
00:45:22,657 --> 00:45:24,292
Thank you.

597
00:45:49,784 --> 00:45:50,952
He will bring me to school?

598
00:45:50,952 --> 00:45:53,154
- Yes.
- No need, Ma'am Serafica.

599
00:45:53,154 --> 00:45:56,591
Grandpa Garp has helped me a lot.

600
00:45:56,591 --> 00:45:59,156
I can go to school on my own,

601
00:45:59,156 --> 00:46:02,438
so I won't disturb you and Mr. James.

602
00:46:02,438 --> 00:46:04,165
I'm rooting for you.

603
00:46:04,165 --> 00:46:05,567
Good luck.

604
00:46:05,567 --> 00:46:08,664
Point me in the right direction.

605
00:46:08,664 --> 00:46:14,042
Or better yet,
make our paths meet so I can save her,

606
00:46:14,042 --> 00:46:17,045
and give her the life you dreamed for her.

607
00:46:17,045 --> 00:46:20,482
Please, Alyanna.

608
00:46:20,482 --> 00:46:23,491
Break a leg and see you at school.

609
00:46:23,491 --> 00:46:27,527
I'm Florence Dela Cruz
and I'm going to school.

610
00:46:40,802 --> 00:46:44,612
What in the name of...
